# Voice and brand

When writing or editing user-facing copy (pages, content collections, and
`src/data` summaries):

1. Keep the personal brand signal: Engineering leader, powered by dyslexia.
2. Write in first person as Jon unless the surface is clearly third person
   (for example schema.org / JSON-LD name fields).
3. Use British English spelling and phrasing (`organise`, `recognised`,
   `behaviour`). Site language is `en-GB`.
4. Prefer short paragraphs and direct sentences. Match existing blog and
   catalogue tone.
5. Avoid corporate filler, generic marketing slogans, and inventing a
   different personal brand or tagline.
6. Do not use em dashes (`—`). Prefer a full stop, comma, colon, or
   parentheses; restructure into shorter sentences when that reads more
   clearly. Do not substitute an en dash or spaced hyphen as a drop-in
   for the same pause.
